+---
+name: verify-plaid-sync-cursor
+description: "Run TLC on the Plaid sync cursor race model when changing plaidStore.persistTransactionsSync, plaid.ts syncTransactionsForItem, or Plaid sync concurrency. Proves stale pages cannot regress the cursor or apply txn payloads after a fresher sync."
+---
+
+# Verify Plaid sync cursor
+
+**Property:** A sync worker that started at cursor `C` must not write
+transactions or move `plaidItems.cursor` unless the stored cursor still
+equals `C` (missing normalized to empty).
+
+**Harm if broken:** Reconciliation, P&L, and bonus spend can use stale
+transactions after concurrent webhook + pull sync.
+
+## Code coverage (sync commit)
+
+| File | Functions |
+| ---- | --------- |
+| `convex/convex/plaidStore.ts` | `plaidSyncCursorsEqual` |
+| `convex/convex/plaidStore.ts` | `persistTransactionsSync` |
+| `convex/convex/plaid.ts` | `syncTransactionsForItem` retry loop |
+
+**Last verified:** commit `5aa459e` (Buggy TLC fail, Fixed TLC pass, plaid 12/12).
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+```bash
+bash runtime/tla/install-tla2tools.sh   # once, if tla2tools.jar missing
+```
+
+## Run (one heavy job at a time)
+
+Buggy model must **fail** (proves properties are real):
+
+```bash
+runtime/tla/bin/tlc \
+  -config runtime/tla/plaid-sync-cursor/PlaidSyncCursorBuggy.cfg \
+  runtime/tla/plaid-sync-cursor/PlaidSyncCursorBuggy.tla
+```
+
+Fixed model must **pass**:
+
+```bash
+runtime/tla/bin/tlc \
+  -config runtime/tla/plaid-sync-cursor/PlaidSyncCursorFixed.cfg \
+  runtime/tla/plaid-sync-cursor/PlaidSyncCursorFixed.tla
+```
+
+Convex regression (cursor guard):
+
+```bash
+cd convex && npm test -- convex/__tests__/plaid.test.ts
+```
+
+## Invariants in TLA+
+
+- `NoStaleWriteAfterAdvance` — no stale apply after cursor advanced.
+- `NoCursorRegression` — stored generation never moves backward.
+
+## Scope limits
+
+- Models generation counter abstraction, not full Plaid page payloads or OCC retries.
+- Does not prove Plaid API correctness or encryption paths.
+- Two-worker interleaving only; add workers if code allows more.
+
+## If TLC fails on Fixed
+
+1. Map counterexample steps to `GuardedPersist` vs `plaidSyncCursorsEqual` in `plaidStore.ts`.
+2. If the trace is impossible in Convex, fix the TLA guard to match code.
+3. If the trace is possible in production, fix product code — do not weaken invariants.
+
+Bump **Last verified at commit** only when Buggy fails, Fixed passes,
+and plaid tests pass.
+
+Use `/maintain-formal-verification-skill` when merges touch covered
+files without a TLC rerun.
