+# Credit usage per cycle
+
+Each `creditUsage` row is keyed by `(userCardId, creditCatalogId, cycleId)`.
+Status is `userOverride ?? algorithmStatus`.
+
+## State diagram
+
+```mermaid
+stateDiagram-v2
+  [*] --> inactive: reconcileCredit, no match
+  inactive --> probable: auto mode, score ≥ 0.4
+  inactive --> needs_review: confirm/manual mode signals
+  probable --> verified: auto score ≥ 0.7 or user override
+  needs_review --> verified: user override / confirm match+posting
+  verified --> inactive: user marks not used
+  verified --> needs_review: user override needs_review
+  inactive --> expired: cycle end job (status patch)
+  expired --> [*]
+  verified --> [*]: cycle rolls
+```
+
+## Transitions
+
+| Status | Event | Guard | Side effects |
+| ------ | ----- | ----- | ------------ |
+| algorithmic | `reconcileCredit` | matchers, mode | set matches, amount |
+| any | `overrideCreditStatus` | owner | inline amount; schedule reconcile |
+| any | `fileTransactionToCredit` | not pending/filed | manual ids, reconcile |
+| `*` | userOverride set | — | reconcile uses override as status |
+
+## Invariants
+
+- A txn id is in at most one other cycle's sets (`claimedTxnIds` filter).
+- User `verified` override captures full catalog amount, even with no matches.
+- `overrideCreditStatus` patches amount inline before reconcile (`credits.ts`).
+
+## Schema statuses
+
+`verified`, `probable`, `needs_review`, `inactive`, `expired` (`schema.ts` creditStatus).
