+# Plaid item connection lifecycle
+
+`plaidItems.status` tracks link health. Only `active` items sync transactions.
+
+## State diagram
+
+```mermaid
+stateDiagram-v2
+  [*] --> active: storePlaidItem / link success
+  active --> login_required: ITEM_LOGIN_REQUIRED webhook
+  active --> revoked: USER_PERMISSION_REVOKED
+  active --> error: ITEM_ERROR / sync failure path
+  active --> removed: user disconnect / deletePlaidItemAndCascade
+  login_required --> active: clearPlaidItemReauth + successful update
+  error --> active: markPlaidItemStatus(active) after fix
+  revoked --> active: fresh Link (storePlaidItem re-link)
+  removed --> [*]
+  revoked --> [*]: item deleted
+```
+
+## Transitions
+
+| Status | Event | Guard | Side effects |
+| ------ | ----- | ----- | ------------ |
+| `active` | `storePlaidItem` | any plaidItemId | encrypt token; append tokens |
+| `active` | `syncTransactionsForItem` | status active | txn pages |
+| `login_required` | Plaid webhook | error code | UI prompts reauth |
+| `active` | `clearPlaidItemReauth` | caller owns item | patch status active |
+| `*` | `deletePlaidItemAndCascade` | — | cascade if last item; delete row |
+| `*` | `markPlaidItemStatus` | item exists | patch status + updatedAt |
+
+## Invariants
+
+- Transaction sync and account listing skip non-`active` items (`plaid.ts` filters).
+- `exchangePublicToken` / update flows reject revoked/removed/error items.
