+# Plaid transaction sync cursor
+
+Concurrent syncs can interleave pages against one `plaidItems` row.
+The stored cursor is the token for compare-and-swap writes.
+
+## State diagram
+
+```mermaid
+stateDiagram-v2
+  [*] --> Idle: item stored
+  Idle --> PageFetch: syncTransactionsForItem reads cursor C
+  PageFetch --> PersistOk: persist expectedCursor=C matches DB
+  PersistOk --> PageFetch: has_more
+  PersistOk --> SyncDone: !has_more
+  PageFetch --> Conflict: expectedCursor ≠ stored cursor
+  Conflict --> RetryOnce: syncTransactionsForItem restarts from fresh cursor
+  Conflict --> Blocked: second conflict in same action
+  RetryOnce --> PageFetch
+  SyncDone --> [*]
+  Blocked --> [*]
+```
+
+## Transitions
+
+| State / step | Event | Guard | Side effects |
+| ------------ | ----- | ----- | ------------ |
+| Idle | `syncTransactionsForItem` | item active, owner match | read cursor |
+| PageFetch | Plaid `/transactions/sync` | — | page of changes |
+| PersistOk | persist | cursors equal | write txns; set `nextCursor` |
+| Conflict | persist | cursor mismatch | return conflict; no txn writes |
+| RetryOnce | action loop | first conflict | re-read cursor, restart pages |
+| Blocked | action loop | second conflict | `reason: "cursor_conflict"` |
+| SyncDone | last page | persist succeeded | reconcile credits + signup bonus |
+
+## Invariants
+
+- Stale pages never regress `plaidItems.cursor`.
+- Stale pages never apply payloads after a fresher sync advanced the cursor.
+- Missing cursor and `undefined` expected cursor compare equal (initial sync).
+
+TLA+ model: `runtime/tla/plaid-sync-cursor/PlaidSyncCursorFixed.tla`.
