+# SRW-1458 check proof
+
+Bot 2 sell and trim reservations, the facade sell count, and the P50 replay.
+P50 re-cut part 5. Refs #1458, ticket #1689.
+
+Source PR #1682 at head `d17cefc84bc84789abcf44c762bea2d2c16bfe6c`.
+
+Tested commit: `04cd5ba3111b890a36912ad71461e5904a09a30d`, the merge of
+`origin/main` (`e30986ff`) into this branch's code head `3c809b98`. Every result
+below was produced on that commit, and the only change after it in this branch is
+this record and `evidence/SRW-1458/receipt.json`, which the replay writes and
+which names that commit as its `implementationSha`.
+
+## Scope
+
+| Path | Why it belongs to this ticket |
+| --- | --- |
+| `bot2/trade_machine.js` | the Bot 2 exit and trim reservation, the terminal observation and the holdings reconcile |
+| `alpaca_paper_execution.js` | `reservedSellQuantity` joins the local order list and the shared hold by client order id |
+| `scripts/srw1458_sell_reservation_proof.cjs` | the three-account replay, plus the two unlinked-floor cases carried from #1740/#1885 |
+| `fixtures/srw1458/replay_input.json` | the frozen replay input |
+| `fixtures/srw1458/replay_expected.json` | the independent expected outcomes, byte for byte from the source PR |
+| `fixtures/srw1458/replay.manifest.json` | the sha256 pins and the runner name |
+| `evidence/SRW-1458/receipt.json` | the receipt the replay writes |
+| `evidence/SRW-1458/facade-sell-count-probe.cjs` | the credential-free probe for overlapping and disjoint facade order ids |
+| `evidence/SRW-1458/check-proof.md` | this record |
+
+Diff size against `origin/main`: 25 added and 3 deleted lines in
+`alpaca_paper_execution.js`, 54 and 2 in `bot2/trade_machine.js`. That is 84
+changed lines across 2 counted code files, against the cap of 150 lines and 3
+files. The proof, the fixtures and this evidence directory are excluded by the
+gate, exactly as the ticket states.
+
+No path outside the ticket's `In:` declaration carries a runtime change. The
+service passes no `sellReservation` handle to `createTradeMachine`, so the
+default exit path, the account and bot isolation and every existing broker order
+identity are unchanged.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **Bot 2 exit send.** A sell reserves `qty` units under its own attempt id and
+  client order id as `unknown` before `submitOrder`. A refusal throws
+  `sell_reservation_refused_<reason>` and never sends.
+- **Bot 2 trim send.** The same reservation, under `trim.client_order_id`, taken
+  after the last admission check and before `submitOrder`.
+- **Exit fill observation.** Every exit order's cumulative fill and status are
+  written to the shared owner, so a replacement leg never re-sells a unit the
+  previous leg already sold. A broker order id that is not a non-empty string is
+  skipped rather than guessed, and a refused observation is logged as
+  `sell_reservation_observe_refused` instead of disappearing.
+- **Holdings reads.** `checkPosition` and the terminal trim position read are the
+  proof the owner needs before it releases anything. A refused `reconcile` is
+  swallowed: the units stay reserved and the exit pass continues. The
+  `position_mismatch` guard still throws exactly as before, on the same `left`
+  value it always compared.
+- **Facade sell count.** `reservedSellQuantity` accumulates the local working
+  sells by client order id in a map, then adds the shared owner's outstanding
+  units for the ids the local list does not count. An id both know is counted
+  once at the larger outstanding, so a lagging local remainder never frees units
+  the owner still holds. A count that is not a nonnegative safe integer is
+  skipped rather than added, so a malformed row never lowers the total. A shared
+  hold with no client order id is keyed by its own reservation id, so two id-less
+  holds stay two holds.
+- **Replay.** `scripts/srw1458_sell_reservation_proof.cjs` runs seven replay cases
+  against the frozen fixtures and pins their sha256, then runs the two
+  unlinked-floor cases that the file already carried on `main`. The receipt names
+  the input and expected hashes, the three identity derivations and the fake
+  partition trace.
+
+## One acceptance half is blocked, and the pin is not weakened
+
+The frozen expected file is the source PR's file, byte for byte, and its pin
+`dd8e10b1fe650ebabcc1a75a673216048c32d17df4f3530aaa9c74ccde67652a` is unchanged.
+Nothing in it was edited to match this build.
+
+The late-fill case then disagrees with it in exactly one place. The design head
+expects the four units the delayed fill leaves to be released on the holdings
+reconcile, and a four-unit replacement sent. P50.1 (#1758, merged as #2285) makes
+a release wait for the broker's terminal fill total for every leg of the family
+plus `RELEASE_SETTLE_MS` after the terminal observation, and the Bot 1 exit
+reducer passes no totals. A terminal sell whose units are held therefore stays
+reserved and no replacement is sent.
+
+The replay records that as **BLOCKED**, not as a pass and not as a corrected
+expectation. The case still compares everything it can prove — the fills, the
+reservations before the reconcile, the duplicate and reordered snapshots, the
+absence of a send before a reconcile — and it asserts that the withheld half
+falls the safe way:
+
+- the delayed fill still books the units the contract says it books (sold 6);
+- the reserved total is at least what the contract releases (4, never less);
+- capacity is at most what the contract releases (0, never invented);
+- the replacement sent is at most what the contract allows (0 of 4).
+
+The receipt carries `{ label: 'lateFill', ok: true, blocked: [afterDelayedFill.released,
+afterDelayedFill.reserved, afterDelayedFill.capacity, replacementQty] }`, so the
+divergence is data in the record rather than a silently changed oracle. Closing
+it needs terminal fill totals from the reducer or a contract revision, which is
+the activation boundary (#1464), not this slice.
