+## Open trades and blast radius
+
+- Capability off: no change from `origin/main`.
+- A trade opened before the capability is on has no `target_ladder` and no frozen marker, so turning the capability on later does not give it a ladder. Its single target and stop keep protecting it.
+- A trade opened with the capability on freezes its rung list and the `target_ladder: true` marker in `lane_config`. A later config revision does not change it.
+- Turning the capability off stops the ladder. The frozen rung list stays on the row for the record, and the single target (the last rung price) and the stop keep protecting it. A working rung is reconciled and finished; an unsent queued rung is superseded.
+- A signal trim and a rung share one `trim_pending`, so only one sell is ever working for a trade.
+- A late entry fill that changes the plan drops the ladder (the plan no longer matches), and the single target and stop protect the row.
+
+## Rollback
+
+Turn off `trading.target_ladder` and let the working rung leg reach a terminal state before reverting. The frozen `target_ladder` and its cumulative fills stay on the row, so a later re-enable resumes from the recorded fills. An old reader ignores `target_ladder`, `target_ladder_dropped` and `target_ladder_exit_rung` and reads the single `target_level`, which the ladder records as its last rung price. P54 (#1464) must qualify that before activation.
+
+## P27b dependency
+
+`bot2/lane_control_schema.js` does not yet accept `targets` or `break_even_after_first`; P27b (#1423) adds those keys and the lane editor fields. Until then a committed lane config cannot carry a ladder, so the freeze in `snapshotLane` is inert in production. The proof drives the frozen `lane_config` directly, which is the same shape P27b will write. This PR does not touch the schema, the editor or the dashboard.
