@@ -0,0 +1,153 @@
+# SRW-1687 check proof
+
+Settle Bot 1 sell orders before replacement. P50 re-cut part 3. Refs #1458.
+
+## Scope
+
+The branch carries a merge of `9163b43b` (main). The only conflict was the
+executor option list, where main added `diskAdmission` and this change added
+`sellReservation`; both are kept. Every check below was re-run on the merged
+head.
+
+The ticket's `In:` declaration names `thala_v2_executor.js`. This change touches
+that file and this evidence file, and nothing else. The evidence file is the
+acceptance record the ticket asks for, not a code file.
+
+| Path | Why it belongs to this ticket |
+| --- | --- |
+| `thala_v2_executor.js` | the optional Bot 1 reservation handle, the sell observation and settlement path, the cumulative floor, and the stall page |
+| `evidence/SRW-1687/check-proof.md` | the acceptance record for the two proofs the ticket names |
+
+Diff size: 134 added and 9 deleted lines in one code file. The gate caps are 150
+added plus deleted lines and 3 counted code files.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `sellReservation` is a new optional executor option, default `null`. No caller
+  in the service passes one, so the intermediate path stays dormant.
+- `advanceSell` observes every sell snapshot into the reservation book
+  (`observeOrder`) before it decides anything, and takes the book's cumulative
+  quantity as a floor. A terminal status never releases units on its own.
+- A terminal sell whose reservation is still held keeps its broker order id and
+  client order id, is marked `settling`, and returns before the replacement and
+  reprice branches. It is read again on the next pass.
+- A settling sell is gated before the cancel, reprice and replacement branches,
+  so a reordered working poll cannot resume any of them.
+- A `filled` poll with a handle goes through the same reconciliation and the
+  same monotonic accounting as every other terminal status.
+- `reconcileSellReservation` reads fresh close evidence when the cached position
+  read predates the terminal observation, and dates the reconcile by when the
+  read was asked for, never by when it answered.
+- `heldReservation` looks the reservation up by the sell's original client order
+  id first, so a broker reprice that mints a child id cannot read as a release.
+- `applySellDelta` applies the cumulative floor to `qtyLeft` and `soldByRef`, so
+  a settling pass still debits the fills it observed and a reordered snapshot
+  never restores a unit. With no handle the ledger moves exactly as before.
+- The no-bid MARKET residual is sized from the applied floor, not the raw
+  snapshot.
+- `brokerSellQty` proves the position it read into the book, so the reservation
+  has a baseline to measure against.
+- A settle that never reconciles raises one owner alert after 60 seconds, and
+  the timer runs on every settling pass, including a failed or deferred read.
+- The sell poll is forced while a sell is settling.
+- A replacement leg resets the settle state it would otherwise inherit, so its
+  own stall timer and its own page are its own.
+
+Reserve-before-send wiring is deliberately absent: no `reserve` call exists in
+the executor. That belongs to the next slice.
+
+## Checks
+
+| Check | Command | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Forced-boundary close proof | `node scripts/thala_v2_close_proof.cjs --forced-boundaries` | `PASS: 50 of 50, zero double sells` and `PASS: 63 of 63, zero double sells` |
+| Credential-free probe | temporary script, fake broker and fake compare-and-swap store | 23 of 23 probes pass |
+| Reservation store proof | `node scripts/srw1458_1_reservation_store_proof.cjs` | 6/6 cases pass |
+| Conservation proof | `node scripts/srw1458_2_reservation_conservation_proof.cjs` | 6/6 cases pass |
+| Counted-orders proof | `node scripts/srw1458_3_counted_orders_proof.cjs` | 12/12 cases pass |
+| Positions proof | `node scripts/srw1332_positions_proof.cjs` | PASS |
+| Day counters proof | `node scripts/srw1399_day_counters_proof.cjs` | 17 checks passed |
+| Flatten settle proof | `node scripts/srw1390_flatten_settle_proof.cjs` | all 9 replays passed |
+| Deferred manual exit proof | `node scripts/srw1391_deferred_manual_exit_proof.cjs` | 19/19 passed |
+| Manual exit posts proof | `node scripts/srw1344_manual_exit_posts_proof.cjs` | 15/15 pass |
+| Third take profit proof | `node scripts/srw1405_third_take_profit_proof.cjs` | PASS |
+| Operator exit plan proof | `node scripts/srw1406_operator_exit_plan_proof.cjs` | PASS |
+| Flatten fixed point proof | `node scripts/srw1468_flatten_fixed_point_proof.cjs` | all 9 replays passed |
+| Sell recovery scope | `node test_srw1309_sell_recovery_scope.js` | PASS |
+| Exit watchdog | `node test_srw1322_exit_watchdog.js` | 24 passed, 0 failed |
+| Exit pass health | `node test_srw1323_exit_pass_health.js` | PASS |
+| Order path review | `node test_srw15_order_path_review.js` | passed |
+| Syntax | `node --check thala_v2_executor.js` | passed |
+| Review scope | `node scripts/srw_review_scope.cjs` | `opus` required for `thala_v2_executor.js` (reason `bot1`); the coordinator's exact-head Astra gate covers it |
+| File-size ratchet | `node scripts/vendor/check-file-size.mjs --base 9163b43b --all-tracked --warn` | warning only, exit 0: `thala_v2_executor.js` was already over the ~8,000 token budget at the base and grew 7,311 bytes |
+| Repository check | `srw/agent-check` on the exact head | published by the Mac check publisher (the merge authority) |
+| Heavy `scripts/check.sh` | not run by the builder | the publisher owns it in this repo |
+| Live-service tests | not run | the reservation handle is disabled in the service; no production caller passes one |
+
+`scripts/srw1457_protection_proof.cjs` was not run to a result: it requires the
+`ws` package, and this worktree has no `node_modules`. That is a missing
+dependency, not a failure of this change.
+
+## What the probe proves
+
+The probe injects a preseeded Bot 1 reservation into the real executor against a
+fake broker. The sell order is already terminal at the broker with one unit
+filled.
+
+- Unavailable holdings: the terminal sell keeps its broker order id and client
+  order id, is marked settling, sends no replacement, and the reservation stays
+  held. The settling pass still debits the one unit it observed.
+- Inconsistent holdings (the broker still reports the whole position): the same
+  identity is retained, the sell is marked settling, no replacement is sent, and
+  the reservation stays held.
+- Reconciled holdings: the reservation releases and the no-bid MARKET fallback
+  replaces the leg, sized from the applied floor (9, not 10).
+- A reordered working poll on a settling sell never reprices it, never replaces
+  it, and never detaches it.
+- A reordered `filled` poll that reports less than the applied floor never
+  restores a unit and never shrinks the leg's credit.
+- A settle that never reconciles pages the owner exactly once, under
+  `sell-settle-stalled:<tradeId>:<clientOrderId>`, and sends no replacement.
+- With no handle injected, the same terminal leg is replaced exactly as before,
+  nothing is marked settling, and no stall page is raised.
+
+## What this does not prove
+
+- The probe is a temporary script and is not committed, so it is not re-run by
+  the repository check. The committed proofs above are.
+- No live broker, credential, or deployment path was exercised. The handle is
+  dormant in the service.
+- The reservation is preseeded by the probe. The executor does not yet reserve
+  before a send, so the probe cannot show that a real send is reserved first.
+  That is the next slice.
+- The forced-boundary proof runs with no handle injected, so it proves the
+  default path is unchanged, not that the settling path survives a process kill.
+- The probe's clock is frozen between passes, so a release needs a pass whose
+  position read is asked for strictly after the terminal observation. In
+  production the two are milliseconds apart and the release lands in the same
+  pass. The probe therefore runs three passes for the release case.
+- The broker reprice path is exercised only through `heldReservation`'s lookup
+  order, not through a real `replaceOrder` that mints a child client order id.
+
+## Carried forward from #1682
+
+The unresolved release, replacement lineage, facade and reducer proof findings
+from #1682 stay open and belong to the activation boundary, not to this slice.
+
+## Self-review
+
+One review pass of the diff ran on `gpt-6.2-astra` (the first unblocked `review`
+entry that is not the builder's own model). It returned five major and two minor
+findings. All seven are fixed in this head.
+
+| Finding | Severity | Fix |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| A reordered working poll could resume the reprice or replacement of a settling sell | major | a settling sell is gated before the cancel, reprice and replacement branches, and the stall timer runs on that gate too |
+| A `filled` poll bypassed settlement and could reverse the ledger | major | with a handle, `filled` goes through the same reconciliation and the same monotonic accounting as every other terminal status |
+| The executor discarded the book's cumulative floor | major | `observeOrder`'s `cumulativeQty` is taken as a floor for the quantity this pass applies |
+| A broker reprice could hide the original reservation | major | `heldReservation` looks up the sell's original client order id first |
+| A pre-terminal position read could look fresh enough to release units | major | the reconcile is dated by when the read was asked for, not by when it answered |
+| A replacement inherited the previous leg's alert state | minor | the replacement leg resets `settling`, `settlingSinceMs`, `terminalObservedAtMs` and `settleAlertedAtMs` |
+| The null-handle path changed | minor | the cumulative floor and the floor-sized residual are gated on the injected handle, so the default path is unchanged |
+
+Nothing was left unfixed. No finding was rejected.
