@@ -0,0 +1,89 @@
+# SRW-1795 check proof
+
+Ticket: shyamsivakumar/strategy-replay-workbench#1795 (P49 piece 2 of 10, the
+exit drill's recording fake broker).
+
+Checked commit: `49bb5cb00a5db678a1a8d1e78b9326a02ab8469a`, the implementation
+head of this pull request. The head of this pull request differs from it by this
+file only, so every result below describes the code that is on the pull request
+head.
+
+The heavy `scripts/check.sh` gate was run on that head from a clean checkout, and
+it passed: `CHECK: PASS 49bb5cb00a5db678a1a8d1e78b9326a02ab8469a`, 28 of 28 hard
+stops, the complete boot manifest, 98 seconds. The Mac check publisher also posts
+`srw/agent-check` on the ready pull request, and the coordinator requires that
+exact-SHA status before merge. The checks below are the ones this change can run
+locally without Docker, a credential or a network.
+
+## What the change does
+
+`scripts/srw_exit_drill.cjs` gains `createRecordingBroker`: a credential-free
+fake broker that answers Bot 1's executor and Bot 2's trade machine from the one
+recorded snapshot, records every call at the dispatch boundary, turns a scripted
+refusal into a refusal on both surfaces, and models a cancel race with a scripted
+status sequence. The budget is injected, not owned here. The file is inert: no
+I/O, no network, no environment read and no order path at require time, and no
+module imports it yet.
+
+## Checks run
+
+| Check | Command | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Ticket proof | `node -e "const m=require('./scripts/srw_exit_drill.cjs'); const b=m.createRecordingBroker({snapshot:{positions:[],orders:[],quotes:{},underlying:{price:1}},clock:()=>0}); if(typeof b.submitOrder!=='function'\|\|typeof b.getOptionQuote!=='function'\|\|typeof b.optionQuotes!=='function'\|\|typeof b.getOrder!=='function')process.exit(1)"` | passed, exit 0 |
+| Red signature | the same command on the pre-change file | `TypeError: m.createRecordingBroker is not a function` |
+| Syntax | `node --check scripts/srw_exit_drill.cjs` | passed |
+| Piece 1 regression | `credentialPath`, `normalizeClock` and `validateScenario` re-exercised | passed |
+| Review scope | `node scripts/srw_review_scope.cjs` | `unknown-executable` note for a new `scripts/*.cjs`; not a check failure |
+| Behaviour proof | a temp-dir script, since deleted, exercising the real path | passed |
+
+The behaviour proof covered, at `49bb5cb0`:
+
+- **One snapshot answers both surfaces.** Bot 1's `getOrder` returns the order or
+  `null`; Bot 2's `orderById`/`orderByClientId` return a found/absent envelope.
+  `getOptionQuote` returns one quote or `null`; `optionQuotes` returns a map.
+  `submitOrder` returns the order on Bot 1 and `{ok, status, order}` on Bot 2.
+  `getEquity`, `getUnderlyingPrice`, `getCloseEvidence`, `positions`, `calendar`,
+  `openOrders`, `underlyingQuote`, `requestRate`, `paperIdentity`, `guard` and
+  `paperBase` all answer from the same snapshot.
+- **Every call is recorded with its class, client order id, quantity and answer.**
+  All seventeen call classes appear in `calls`, every row carries the four fields
+  with `null` where a field does not apply, and no row has a `null` answer.
+  `paperIdentity` and `requestRate` are recorded too.
+- **A scripted refusal is a refusal.** Bot 2 gets `{ok: false, status, message}`
+  and no order is created and no position moves; Bot 1 gets a thrown error with
+  `status` and `thalaSellRefusal: true`. The trace records `answer: 'refused'`.
+- **A working or partial status is honoured.** `status: 'new'` returns a `new`
+  order with `filled_qty: '0'` and moves nothing; `partially_filled` with
+  `filledQty: 1` of 2 moves the position by one. An unsupported status, a
+  partial fill that is not a strict part, a partial fill with no quantity and a
+  `filled` status whose quantity contradicts the order are all refused before
+  any state moves.
+- **A scripted status sequence models a cancel race on both surfaces.** The
+  sequence is copied per order on first read and shared by `getOrder`,
+  `findOrderByClientId`, `orderById` and `orderByClientId`. The cancel is
+  acknowledged, the order reads `canceled`, the next read reports `filled`, the
+  position moves once, and a repeated read is not a second fill.
+- **A generated order id never overwrites a seeded one.** With a seeded
+  `drill-order-1`, the first submit takes `drill-order-2` and the seeded order
+  stays reachable by client id.
+- **A quote without a recorded observation time is unavailable.** A snapshot
+  quote with no `atMs` returns `null` from `getOptionQuote` and is absent from
+  `optionQuotes`, so a recorded bid cannot pass a freshness check forever.
+- **`getCloseEvidence` returns the symbol's orders with its position**, which is
+  the shape `thala_v2_executor.js` reads at the close-evidence adoption path.
+- **A budget refusal is recorded and sends nothing.** Bot 2 gets the 429
